      "connector-runner e2e 2026-10-18 (gettakaro/connectors#519): real vanilla Valheim PC client (Steam, Version 1.0.20 n-41) on this exact pin (server files sha256-checked against inputs.server.files), plugin built from this branch through hosted Takaro MCP - player-connected b332e352-af90-4004-af5f-53a3b8471395, chat-message 7eafae09-343f-4573-be68-3d459b5f87f6, player-death 954767e3-21b8-4b28-83db-4fe5d9568464, command-executed @ping e4e237bd-3ee5-4cf8-98cc-fbc45dc52c16, player-disconnected a0647a28-19db-4fc2-888e-83c099b84191; testReachability, getPlayers, sendMessage (with senderNameOverride), executeConsoleCommand (allowlisted help, denial of a non-allowlisted command, allowlisted kick), teleportPlayer, giveItem, kickPlayer, banPlayer/listBans/unbanPlayer (banned rejoin refused, rejoin after unban) and shutdown seen in the client; Discord chat bridge game-to-Discord and Discord-to-game relays and connect/disconnect posts; not re-proven on this pin: entity-killed"
    ],
    "notes": "Exact Steam pin of the public head at declaration time (buildid 25909431, Valheim 1.0.20 network version 41, updated 2026-10-15). Repins the previous 1.0.17/25730807 target after Valve moved the public branch (#519); depot 896661 manifest 4001404753685205688. The connector is a dedicated-server plugin. An optional graphical-client inventory mod (role client-companion) exists; deploy only parks its zip in takaro-companion/. Player-driven events (chat, deaths, kills), server chat and the optional inventory mod need a connected game client and are NOT covered by takaro-maint verify, which boots a dedicated server with no client. Runtime CI onboarding is a separate issue."
  },
